IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mwa-types`
IMPORT `mwa-rates`
IMPORT `mwa-payment`
IMPORT `mwa-enforcement`

-- Minimum Wage Act 1983 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this worker and this pay period: does the Act apply; which minimum
--    rate governs and what is it per hour; what is the minimum for the
--    period; what may be deducted for board and lodging; and how much is
--    owed?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1 and 2 (mwa-rates.l4, mwa-payment.l4).
-- Enforcement, hours, and administration (Goals 3-5) answer their own
-- questions in mwa-enforcement.l4.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Minimum wage position` HAS
    `the Act applies`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rate that governs`                             IS A `Rate that governs`
    `minimum rate per hour`                             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `hours the minimum applies to`                      IS A NUMBER
    `minimum wages for the period`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `board and lodging deductions that count`           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `a deduction exceeds what s 7(1) allows`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `arrears owed`                                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover the arrears (s 11)` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 2, 4, 4A, 4B, 6, 7, 8(4), 9, 11
@export default The minimum wage position of a worker for a pay period under the Minimum Wage Act 1983 (NZ): whether the Act applies (ss 2, 9); which minimum rate governs — an exemption permit (s 8(4)), a starting-out rate (s 4A), the training rate (s 4B) or the adult rate (s 4) — and what it is per hour; the minimum for the period (s 6); the board and lodging deductions that count, and whether a deduction exceeds what s 7(1) allows; the arrears owed; and whether they may be recovered under s 11. The rates are the Minimum Wage Order's, supplied by the caller. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Wage case`  @desc The worker, the Minimum Wage Order in force (its adult, starting-out and training rates per hour), and the pay period (hours engaged, time lost, travel between clients, board and lodging, wages paid in money)
GIVETH A `Minimum wage position`
`the minimum wage position for` c MEANS
    `Minimum wage position` WITH
        `the Act applies`                               IS `the Act applies to` (c's `worker`)
        `the rate that governs`                         IS rate
        `minimum rate per hour`                         IS hourly
        `hours the minimum applies to`                  IS hours
        `minimum wages for the period`                  IS minimum
        `board and lodging deductions that count`       IS
            CONSIDER minimum
            WHEN JUST m THEN JUST (`the board and lodging deductions that count, under` (c's `period`'s `board and lodging`) `from` m)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `a deduction exceeds what s 7(1) allows`        IS
            CONSIDER minimum
            WHEN JUST m THEN `a board or lodging deduction exceeds what s 7(1) allows, under` (c's `period`'s `board and lodging`) `from` m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        `arrears owed`                                  IS arrears
        `the worker or a Labour Inspector may recover the arrears (s 11)` IS
            CONSIDER arrears
            WHEN JUST a THEN `may recover the wages under s 11` `the worker` `, s 11 applies:` (`s 11 applies` FALSE (a GREATER THAN 0)) `, accepted:` FALSE `, agreed otherwise:` FALSE `, conduct on` (c's `period`'s `last day of the period`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        rate    MEANS `the rate that governs` (c's `worker`) `under` (c's `order`) `on` (c's `period`'s `last day of the period`)
        hourly  MEANS `the hourly minimum under` rate
        hours   MEANS `the hours the minimum applies to` (c's `worker`) (c's `period`)
        minimum MEANS `the minimum wages at` hourly `for hours` hours
        arrears MEANS `the arrears at` hourly `for` (c's `worker`) `in` (c's `period`)
